+/// Rows at or below this use the small-row form: the maxima over the pool's own 2D grid (block_max), then the selection
+/// from those global maxima in one CTA a row (tf_ds_idx_pick_kernel), because a single CTA a row leaves most of the GPU
+/// idle at one to seven rows. Above it the one-launch fused form runs. Both produce the same block list.
+pub const small_rows = 7;
+/// The block count from which the small-row form pays: at the pool's 8192-block cap (65,536 columns) the 2D grid's
+/// parallel score read wins at both one and seven rows (10.5 vs 12.1 µs, 11.8 vs 12.4 µs); at 2048 and 4096 blocks the
+/// second launch and the selection's staging cost more than the parallel read saves (5.8 vs 5.6, 8.7 vs 8.5 µs).
+pub const small_nbk = 6144;
